    "result_text": "I've made the person's grade dated, and `bin/e2e` builds the app and passes all 4 tests in the spec.\n\n**Stored data:** a new migration, `V23__person_grade_dated.sql`, adds a `person_grade` table that holds each person's grades with their from-dates. Existing grades are moved into it as applying from the beginning of time, and the old `person.grade` column is dropped. There is at most one grade per from-date; saving another grade for the same date replaces it.\n\n**Server:**\n- **Saving a person:** adding someone records their first grade from the beginning of time. Each edit records the grade from the form's from-date (the sheet's today if none is given) and keeps the grades already recorded.\n- **Claims:** a claim's rate comes from the grade in force on the claim's date. This applies to rollups, statements and the clerk settle limit.\n- **The list:** the person shown in the list carries the grade in force on the sheet's today, plus their full list of dated grades.\n- **Audit:** the `PERSON_ADDED` and `PERSON_EDITED` lines are unchanged. They show the grade that was submitted and have no new fields.\n\n**Front end:** the person form has a new \"Grade from\" date input (`person-form-grade-from`) that defaults to the sheet's today. The list, the claim dues and the period totals now all look up the grade by date.\n\n**One rule change you should know about:** a person's due-total used to show \"n/a\" whenever their current grade had no rate today and none of their claims kept a fixed figure. The first test requires a total of 3.00 in exactly that case: Ada moves to grade C, which has no rate, but her older claims still have dues under grades A and B. So it now shows \"n/a\" only when the current grade has no rate today **and** none of their counting claims has a due. Statements use the same rule. As a side effect, a claim dated in the future under a rate that starts in the future now adds to the total where it used to show \"n/a\".\n\n**Not done:** the request says an import line gives its grade from the sheet's today, but the app has no import feature, so there was nothing to change. Quick-add still creates a new person with grade A from the beginning of time, as their first grade.",
